Later in the afternoon, I walk down to the local supermarket.
I need to buy groceries for tonight.
I find some fresh, red tomatoes and a bag of beans.
I also need some strong spices.
I pay at the register and walk home again.
My kitchen is small, but it is very cozy.
I put my bags on the table and wash my hands.
I am going to make a large batch of traditional Mexican stew.
It is one of my mother's old recipes.
I take out my wooden board and a sharp knife.
I spend a relaxing hour in the kitchen.
It is nice to stand and chop vegetables.
I cut the tomatoes and onions into small pieces.
The smells remind me of my home in Mexico.
But now it is also my home here in Copenhagen.
I put it all into a large pot on the stove.
The stew has to stand and simmer slowly.
I stir it and taste the sauce with a spoon.
It tastes absolutely perfect.
I am really looking forward to eating dinner with Nina.
